# Level 1, and the point of it is **two pickups of two different items.**
#
# Every movie before this one contains exactly one pickup, it is collision id
# $0C, and its inventory slot is 0 -- so `$80:F87B`'s slot arithmetic agreed
# with every wrong version of itself (`index / 2 - $0C` and `index - $18` are
# both 0 when the id is the first one), and both of its other two branches were
# untaken: the one pickup leaves through the auto-select tail rather than the
# routine's own `RTS`, and $99 added to an empty counter needs no decimal
# adjust. Three perturbations of a ported routine passed because of that.
#
# What this movie does is walk Zeke over two of level 1's nine objects. The
# object list is placement data (`zamn_assets actors <rom> 2`) and the type ->
# collision id table is `$80:CA30`, indexed by the object's type byte, which is
# already doubled:
#
#     obj  type  position      id    $80:F808 entry
#      6   $16   (251, 302)   $12    $80:F87B  pickup, slot 6   <- first
#      0   $00   (307, 135)   $0C    $80:F87B  pickup, slot 0   <- second
#      1   $08   (128, 310)   $21    $80:F8D6  not ported
#      5   $34   (351,  71)   $2D    $80:FA26  not ported
#
# Object 6 is the one that settles the arithmetic: its slot is 6, so the two
# ways of computing it differ ($0C vs $06) and the diff can finally tell them
# apart. Object 0 is the one that settles the BCD: slot 0 starts the level at
# $0150 and the table at `$80:F8AC` pays $0099, and $50 + $99 carries a digit --
# which you can read off the HUD, where the ammo counter goes 150 -> 249.
#
# The route matters more than it looks, because `$80:BEE1` is a 16x16 box on
# the two records' own coordinates: eight pixels either way, which is four
# frames of walking. Zeke goes left along the foot of the pool enclosure and
# then straight up the outside of its left hedge, which puts him through object
# 6 without ever coming near object 1 (the key at (128,310), whose id is not
# ported and would show up as a decline). Object 0 sits just above a bench, and
# the bench is solid -- walking north into it stops him ten pixels short -- so
# the last four lines go round its right end, up, back left over the top of it
# and down onto the item.
#
# Nothing is fired here and nothing is rescued; this movie is one thing.
#
# The boot prefix through frame 1484 is level1.zmv's, unchanged.
#
# Retune by watching where it actually gets to:
#   zamn_headless <rom> shot.png 2300 -m movies\level1-pickups.zmv --at 2100,2252

